  "id": "COMPOUND:30169 - PROTEIN:5836",
  "verbalization": "Leosibirone B, (rel)- is implicated in the interaction with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, a protein that is targeted by multiple complex compounds, including (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan. These compounds are all linked to HUVEC, a human vascular endothelial cell line, suggesting a potential role for Leosibirone B in modulating the activity of this enzyme in HUVEC cells. The evidence suggests that Leosibirone B may act through a complex pathway involving multiple targets, with HUVEC being a downstream effector in this network. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase as a central mediator in the interaction between Leosibirone B and HUVEC, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
